BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Crime and Cuisine on Federal Hill
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261128
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261129
DTSTAMP:20261126T194810Z
UID:3669971edf490fcc4fcfa22250b5@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:A food tour with a felonious twist! The Federal Hill neighborh
 ood of Providence is one of its hottest destinations\, home to some of the
  best Italian food in the world. This tour will give you a smorgasbord of 
 its best bites and drinks\, from fine wines to housemade pasta. Come hungr
 y! ​The Hill was also home to some historic characters who dabbled on th
 e wrong side of the law. Follow the intrigue of State v. Patriarca\, when 
 a future mayor took on a mob boss\; learn about the corruption that brough
 t Rhode Island's banking system to its knees in the '90s\, and about a rai
 d on an illegal dice game that sent a Providence Police Officer through a 
 second-story window. Every guest will also get a memento from their time o
 n the Hill to take home with them. Spoiler alert: it's delicious! ​ Gues
 ts under 21 will not be served alcohol on this tour.\n\nSource: https://ww
 w.visitrhodeisland.com/event/crime-and-cuisine-on-federal-hill/112625/
LOCATION:Providence Tour Company\, 99 Atwells Ave\, Providence\, RI 02909
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/crime-and-cuisine-on-federal-hi
 ll/112625/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Early Bird Museum Highlight Tour at Newport Car Museum
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261128
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261129
DTSTAMP:20261126T194810Z
UID:99897d32cd6478342a9bf99f4d21@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Early Bird Highlight Tour For 90 minutes (8:30 &#8211\; 10:00 
 AM) prior to Museum opening. Call to book: +1 (401) 848-2277 Price $75.00 
 per person (minimum 2\, maximum 6 ppl) Offered Wednesday\, Thursday\, and 
 Saturday only April 1 - December 31\, 2026. General admission is included 
 with price. 72-hour advance notice is suggested. Only one group will be ho
 sted on any given morning. This is your chance to have the Newport Car Mus
 eum all to yourself with a private guide to share with you the not-to-miss
  highlights in seven expansive galleries. With over 100 iconic\, rare and 
 exotic cars on display at one time\, this private collection is bursting w
 ith history\, provenance and color\, not to mention the breathtaking sculp
 tural beauty of automotive designs starting with the 1950s and finishing w
 ith new models from the 21 st Century. After 90 minutes with your private
 \, continue to explore at your own pace so that you can further examine yo
 ur favorites from the Ford/Shelby\, Corvette\, World Car\, Porsche\, Fin C
 ar\, American Muscle and Mopar exhibits while enjoying immersive videos\, 
 artwork and the Museum’s eclectic collection of Mid-Century Modern Furni
 ture. Operating hours can also vary based on weather conditions. Call for 
 more details.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/early-bird
 -museum-highlight-tour-at-newport-car-museum/109638/
LOCATION:Newport Car Museum\, Enter at Light 1947 West Main Road\, Portsmo
 uth\, RI 02871
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/early-bird-museum-highlight-tou
 r-at-newport-car-museum/109638/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Foundry Artists Holiday Show
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261128
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261129
DTSTAMP:20261126T194810Z
UID:0d85c26a7522675827fb6270ed81@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:2026 Foundry Artists Holiday Show PAWTUCKET\, RI: The Foundry 
 Artists Association Holiday Show\, one of Rhode Island's premier holiday a
 rt events\, features over 65 professional regional artists. The show is he
 ld at the historic Pawtucket Armory\, located at 172 Exchange Street\, Paw
 tucket\, RI\, and the 44th annual show kicks off with an Opening Night Rec
 eption on Thursday\, December 3 from 5&#8211\;9 p.m. The show will run for
  two full weekends\, Friday through Sunday\, with dates and times as follo
 ws: December 4 from 12&#8211\;8 p.m.\; December 5 from 10 a.m.&#8211\;5 p.
 m.\; December 6 from 10 a.m.&#8211\;5 p.m.\; December 11 from 12&#8211\;8 
 p.m.\; December 12 from 10 a.m.&#8211\;5 p.m.\; and December 13 from 10 a.
 m.&#8211\;5 p.m. Admission and parking are free. There is a handicap-acces
 sible entrance at the rear of the building\, as well as handicap-accessibl
 e facilities in the Armory. Major credit cards are accepted on all purchas
 es. A silent auction showcasing items donated by Foundry artists is a high
 light of the first weekend. This year's auction proceeds will benefit Hope
 Health\, a nonprofit organization that has provided compassionate care to 
 patients and families for 50 years. HopeHealth provides hospice and pallia
 tive care\, caregiver support\, grief support\, and Alzheimer's and dement
 ia care\, helping individuals and families navigate serious illness\, care
 giving\, end-of-life care\, and loss. In addition to funds raised through 
 the silent auction for HopeHealth\, the Foundry Artists Association will c
 ontinue its longstanding tradition of helping those in need in the communi
 ty by collecting canned goods and other non-perishable food donations for 
 the Rhode Island Community Food Bank throughout the two weekends of the sh
 ow. During its long tenure\, this popular and much-anticipated New England
  holiday tradition has offered patrons the opportunity to view and purchas
 e distinctive\, high-quality work from over 65 regional artists selected t
 o participate through a juried process. Categories of fine art and craft r
 ange from art glass to wood and include painting\, sculpture\, metal\, fib
 er\, mixed media\, jewelry\, ceramics\, and photography. With original wor
 k available across a wide range of price points\, visitors can find everyt
 hing from affordable\, one-of-a-kind gifts and small works to significant 
 fine art and statement pieces. The show offers an opportunity to give some
 thing distinctive and handmade while supporting regional artists.\n\nSourc
 e: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/foundry-artists-holiday-show/112
 709/
LOCATION:Pawtucket Armory Arts Center\, 172 Exchange Street\, Pawtucket\, 
 02860
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/foundry-artists-holiday-show/11
 2709/
END:VEVENT
